  "method": "A square grid centred on the nebula, rows toward Galactic north and columns toward increasing longitude. Each cell takes the median brightest-channel value of the screen-size JPEG pixels it covers; cells more than 0.08 above their 3 x 3 median are clipped as star residuals. Cells covered by measured pillars take the glow around them. Emission is luminance from the field's 15th percentile to its peak, raised to the power 1.5; dust marks cells darker than their 9-cell box mean by 0.15-0.5 of it where that glow is at least 0.08-0.2 of the peak, without groups under 4 cells. Both fade out over the outer 0.3 of the inscribed circle's radius.",
